{"description":"Survey MCP protocol versions in the wild (2024-11-05 baseline vs 2025-03-26 vs 2025-06-18) across the target client ecosystems (opencode, Claude, Codex): which versions clients announce/support, server-negotiation behavior per spec, and upgrade cost for eka-mcp. Output: recommendation whether to stay pinned at 2024-11-05 for the production milestone or move to a newer baseline, with the conformance-suite impact and migration steps.","investigationNotes":"Context: eka-mcp pins protocol 2024-11-05 (req:eka-mcp-production MUST). MCP spec moves fast; the production milestone must not accumulate protocol debt unknowingly. Investigation (2026-08-19): opencode announces 2025-06-18 (TS SDK, supports down to 2024-11-05); Claude Code/Desktop announce 2025-11-25 (tolerant downward — verified via Lens Studio and Figma negotiation cases); Codex announces 2025-06-18 (rmcp KNOWN_VERSIONS includes 2024-11-05; 2026-07-28 support rolling out). eka-mcp server.go:28 pins const ProtocolVersion = \"2024-11-05\" but handleInitialize echoes the client's announced version — the const is only the fallback. Subset wire-identical across revisions; no prompts/sampling/logging/elicitation implemented.","conclusion":"STAY at 2024-11-05 for the production milestone. All target clients (opencode, Claude Code/Desktop, Codex) tolerate a server answering with a lower protocol version — 2024-11-05 is in every client's supported list — and eka-mcp implements only a stdio subset (initialize/ping/tools/resources) that is wire-identical across 2024-11-05 → 2025-11-25. The server's echo behavior (answers the client's announced version; the const is only the fallback when the client announces none) already maximizes compatibility; the const should be reframed as the minimum baseline, not a strict pin. Conformance suite (sto:mcp-hardening-conformance) must assert the ACTUAL behavior: initialize echoes client versions (2024-11-05 / 2025-03-26 / 2025-06-18 / 2025-11-25), baseline 2024-11-05 fallback when the client announces none, capabilities limited to tools+resources (no prompts/logging/completions/elicitation claims), JSON-RPC error codes (-32700/-32600/-32601/-32602/-32002/-32003), stdio newline framing, plus an interop smoke against real opencode / Claude Code / Codex clients. Moving baseline (e.g. 2025-06-18) remains possible later via a supported-versions list with min(client, server-latest) negotiation; 2026-07-28 (stateless core, server/discover) is out of scope until target clients ship stable support."}